+**Pitfalls and Edge Cases**
+*   **Discreteness Artifacts:** The precalculated weights are discrete, which can cause artifacts. A 6-bit resolution for fractional parts is used to make these artifacts invisible to the viewer [S1].
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** The memory controller must correctly handle addresses outside the data cube by returning 0 [S1].
+*   **Memory Conflicts:** The hardware design specifically addresses conflict-free access to the 8 neighbors; improper addressing would degrade performance [S1].
 
